TEXT 48 672 Left 2 !.dc temp -40 125 5
TEXT 48 832 Left 2 ;Current-mode (Banba) bandgap reference for a 1.2 V supply. The error amplifier holds a and b equal, so Q1 and Q2 carry equal currents\nand R1 sees dVbe = VT ln 8. Each core branch carries I = Vbe / R2 + VT ln(8) / R1, a falling and a rising part that cancel when\nR2 / R1 is about 7, and R3 turns the same current into vref = R3 (Vbe / R2 + VT ln(8) / R1), about 0.6 V. The ratios set vref, not the\nabsolute values, so process spread mostly cancels. Q3, M11 and M12 start it: in the state with no current, a is low and M12 pulls g down.\nTune the slope over temperature with R2A and R2B (smaller R2 adds the falling Vbe part) and the level with R3.
